{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/681341-soma","id":681341,"title":"Soma","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-28T13:22:42-07:00","id":681341,"title":"Soma","content":"And the reward for most inspirational Descent related visuals and (to a lesser extent) story in a video games goes to....<br /> <br /> Agree or disagree? Discuss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T13:53:04-07:00","id":681381,"title":"","content":"Eh, I'd sooner go Devil May Cry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T14:22:26-07:00","id":681396,"title":"","content":"I thought they were more like Pandorans, or Wretched Prometheans.<br /> <br /> Mostly from an Angel point of view in Descent, I'd use Bayonetta angels.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T14:50:49-07:00","id":681415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/681341-soma?p=681381#post681381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, I'd sooner go Devil May Cry.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'll be honest, I don't see it. Possible I'm too hung up on the spider-scorpion made out of lava, but the plot not-withstanding I don't recall much of that game striking me as particularly &quot;God-Machine&quot;. As blasphemous as it might be to say, I don't even recall anything especially memorable in terms of demons. Had some neat boss fights, and Dante was certainly a badass, but....eh. Like I said, can't recall anything too inspiring in there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T14:56:47-07:00","id":681424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/681341-soma?p=681396#post681396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought they were more like Pandorans, or Wretched Prometheans.<br /> <br /> Mostly from an Angel point of view in Descent, I'd use Bayonetta angels.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I associate Prometheans and Pandorans with...older robots, you know? Golems, deformed monstrosities, that kinda stuff. Demon to me occupies that odd little niche of horror high-tech. Stuff like Alien Isolation and maybe System Shock (Bioshock, on the other hand, screams Promethean to me). <br /> <br /> I am with you on Bayonetta, although mostly for the freakish designs of the Paradiso and Inferno enemies. The game is way too tongue in cheek to be scary on its own (IMHO).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T14:57:10-07:00","id":681425,"title":"","content":"And I don't find anything angelic or demonic in Soma. So, agree to disagree.<br /> <br /> The thing with the God-Machine is that its half-religion, half-machine. So, you really need both halves if you're going to feel like inspirational material to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T16:38:29-07:00","id":681543,"title":"","content":"Not as much for demonic or angelic forms per se, or <i>specific</i> mapping as to which is God and which is the Devil, but...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=D6JGA4xSudU\" data-code=\"D6JGA4xSudU\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/D6JGA4xSudU/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <i>Unmask your heart, and show us your smile.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T17:26:44-07:00","id":681584,"title":"","content":"Fantastic game, Stupid Loserman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T08:43:31-07:00","id":682113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/681341-soma?p=681415#post681415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'll be honest, I don't see it. Possible I'm too hung up on the spider-scorpion made out of lava, but the plot not-withstanding I don't recall much of that game striking me as particularly &quot;God-Machine&quot;. As blasphemous as it might be to say, I don't even recall anything especially memorable in terms of demons. Had some neat boss fights, and Dante was certainly a badass, but....eh. Like I said, can't recall anything too inspiring in there.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which are we talking about, here? The DMC reboot had demons running human society behind the scenes, They Live-style. I can see how that's pretty God-Machiney. Not so much the original games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T10:31:18-07:00","id":682203,"title":"","content":"Probably DMC.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/736x/8a/de/82/8ade82707a5d4b72782b2e6606035ec8.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> That's some concept art for some of their antagonists and I could see that fitting for Angels.<br /> <br /> I used some of the enemies from Devil May Cry....2? One with the tower of the seven sins, to represent ghosts. Good games, those. Looking forward to the Wraith KS book getting here to do something more with that.<br /> <br /> Maybe it's just me, but the thing I always think of when someone brings up Demon is Transformers. Robots in disguise and all. Most Demons don't turn into vehicles without possessing them but in Beast Wars you had them turning into animals and dinosaurs, so humans isn't a big leap.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/681341-soma?p=681424#post681424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I associate Prometheans and Pandorans with...older robots, you know? Golems, deformed monstrosities, that kinda stuff. Demon to me occupies that odd little niche of horror high-tech. Stuff like Alien Isolation and maybe System Shock (Bioshock, on the other hand, screams Promethean to me).</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand, I just don't feel the same way. The 'robots' in Soma were <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">essentially just robots imbued with life,</div></div> </div> </div> which is a very Promethean kind of thing. I mentioned Pandorans and the Wretched because they're very specifically failed Prometheans. But the Unfleshed don't have to be ancient robots, either.<br /> <br /> I suppose some of the Warmachine warjacks might fit, too.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://images.frpgames.org/products/product_67232.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-29-2015, 01:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"dat